    "description": "<blockquote><p><strong>Requirements:</strong> you must have mastered the <strong>Monk</strong> Class.</p></blockquote><p>You learn the ultimate <strong>Monk</strong> spell: <strong>Beaded Weapon</strong>.</p><table><tbody><tr><td style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Beaded Weapon</strong></td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>MP:</strong> 40</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Target:</strong> One equipped weapon</td><td style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Duration:</strong> Scene</td></tr></tbody></table><ul><li><p>At any moment, if you have a full set of active <strong>Soul Beads</strong>, you may spend 40 MP and imbue one equipped weapon with them. Until this spell ends, the weapon gains a <strong>+3 bonus</strong> to Accuracy Checks, and its damage ignores Resistances.</p></li><li><p>If it’s a <strong>melee</strong> weapon, it also gains the <strong>ranged</strong> property, and its attacks can now be launched from afar.</p></li><li><p>If you have that weapon equipped while casting this spell, you may perform a free attack with it as part of the same action.</p></li><li><p>You lose access to <strong>Soul Beads</strong> used, and they don’t count toward the <strong>Clarity Skill</strong> while imbued in your weapon.</p></li><li><p>You can generate <strong>Soul Beads</strong> as normal from the the next turn onwards.</p></li><li><p>Only one weapon can benefit from this Skill at a time.</p></li></ul><p>Add the @UUID[Compendium.fabula-ultima-homebrew.homebrew-skills.Item.9lJf06RynqAfPxXe]{Beaded Weapon} spell to your character sheet.</p>",
